{
  "dom_id": "step-29247",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Applying a Combined Stretch to a Point",
  "problem": "The point $(2,5)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $-2.$ What is the resulting point?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(2x,y\\right).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $-2$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(x,-2y\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left({\\color{blue}2}x,{\\color{red}-2}y\\right).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(2,5) \\mapsto \\left(2\\cdot 2, \\, -2\\cdot5 \\right) = (4,-10).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221743/assets/0d050ec1579f2ea2b37c01f2d7b60fd6580b6bc4766fcdd66005e1c2c103b8c7.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
